A component with state of its own and a slot declared with an argument,
populated by name under a reactive `for`, on every target.

Under a `for` a component with state is built at run time, and a population
written by name there used to be refused. `Card` loops over state of its own
and inserts `cell(r)` once per row, so what each copy renders reads two scopes
at once: `row` is the callee's, bound where `Card` inserts the slot, and `i` is
the caller's loop variable.

html, fyne and gtk4 build a factory or record from the declaration alone, so
passInstanceSlots gives the instantiation a copy of `Card` with the population
spliced in at the insertion. `row` is bound to `r` inside the copy; `i` crosses
as a prop the render writes per copy (`__p0`), and the effect's `@mount`
becomes an event whose body stays in the page's loop -- handed the key it was
mounted with, which is what the relay's argument is. android passes the
population as a composable parameter taking the slot's argument, and
bubbletea splices `Card` with a cell per copy, so the population is written
where it stands.

The second loop hands `Card` nothing, so its insertion renders the fallback
block: the copy-less declaration on html, fyne and gtk4, and a null composable
on android, which used to render nothing at all.

The test runs on every target: two cards mount two cells each, in their own
scope, and adding an item mounts a third card whose cells read `3`.

deny out/none/html/index.html `String\(row\)` -- the population's parameter is bound where the copy inserts it; a bare `row` names nothing in the factory
deny out/go/fyne/model.go `fmt\.Sprint\(row\)` -- as above, for the fyne record
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `fmt\.Sprint\(row\)` -- as above, for the gtk4 record
deny out/none/html/index.html `__prop___on0\(\)` -- the mount hands its key on; an empty relay drops the payload the handler reads
deny out/kotlin/android/app/src/main/java/test/sngl/app/MainScreen.kt `slotContent|cell: @Composable \(Int\) -> Unit = \{\}` -- a slot is a nullable composable of its own, so an unsupplied one renders the fallback
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:test"
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
    none {
        html
    }
}

component Card(start int, cell list[component(row int) node]) node {
    var rows = [start, start + 10]

    vbox {
        button(text="more", @click { rows.push(start + 100) })
        for var r = rows {
            cell(r) {
                text(value="empty")
            }
        }
    }
}

component main node {
    var items = [1, 2]
    var mounted = ""

    vbox {
        button #add(text="add", @click { items.push(3) })
        for var i = items {
            Card(start=i) {
                component cell(row) {
                    text(value="item {i} row {row}")
                    effect(on="{i}:{row}", @mount(k) { mounted = mounted + k + " " })
                }
            }
        }
        for var i = items {
            Card(start=i)
        }
    }
}

func testEachCopyRendersItsOwnCells(t Test, c main) {
    t.assert(c.mounted == "1:1 1:11 2:2 2:12 ")
    c.add.click()
    t.assert(c.mounted == "1:1 1:11 2:2 2:12 3:3 3:13 ")
}

window {
    main
}
